WEBVTT

00:00:59.639 --> 00:01:02.433
That's my kind of world today.

00:01:02.934 --> 00:01:05.228
Excuse the rather bad hairstyle.

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:06.729
(Laughter)

00:01:06.771 --> 00:01:08.356
But I didn't start out like that.

00:01:08.397 --> 00:01:10.900
I actually started out,
before I became a journalist,

00:01:10.942 --> 00:01:14.278
as a cultural anthropologist,
looking like this.

00:01:14.278 --> 00:01:16.114
(Laughter)

00:01:16.114 --> 00:01:20.284
I did fieldwork, as we call it,
in Soviet Tajikistan,

00:01:20.326 --> 00:01:22.620
on the borders of Afghanistan.

00:01:22.995 --> 00:01:28.209
Now, what cultural anthropology does
is try to study human culture,

00:01:28.251 --> 00:01:31.921
all the assumptions that we inherit
from our surroundings